4dad55f343cad9490ed05341d95b82529","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stellarshenson/jupyterlab_colourful_tab_extension/commits/1f2fb244dad55f343cad9490ed05341d95b82529"}],"sha":"2e4879f10990a489e45aab9361d73c380459c72f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stellarshenson/jupyterlab_colourful_tab_extension/commits/2e4879f10990a489e45aab9361d73c380459c72f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18424023?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/stellarshenson","id":18424023,"login":"stellarshenson","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDI0MDIz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stellarshenson/jupyterlab_colourful_tab_extension/commits/1f2fb244dad55f343cad9490ed05341d95b82529/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-05T07:49:50Z","email":"konrad.jelen@gmail.com","name":"stellarshenson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-05T07:49:50Z","email":"konrad.jelen@gmail.com","name":"stellarshenson"},"message":"feat: tab colour ownership API and terminal fingerprint server extension\n\nA terminal tab could inherit the colour of a terminal that had already\nclosed. The server hands a closed terminal''s name to the next terminal\ncreated, and a colour stored under that name survived every prune,\nbecause the prune drops entries absent from the running list and a\nrecycled name is present in it.\n\nIColourfulTabs gains two members. colourChanged is emitted from the two\nmenu command handlers for every pick and every clear, carrying the colour\nid rather than the palette index so the palette can be reordered without\nbreaking a consumer; it is the only way to learn of a choice, since a\nstored value is a leftover rather than evidence of a click. claim(widget)\ndeclares that another extension persists a tab''s colour - a claimed tab\nis never written to localStorage, a pick on one deletes what was stored\nfor it before, and claims are reference counted.\n\nA new jupyter_server extension serves GET colourful-tab/terminals,\nanswering the pty incarnation behind each terminal name as pid paired\nwith the process start time from /proc/<pid>/stat field 22, split after\nthe last '')'' so a comm containing parentheses cannot shift the fields.\nThe registry is read directly: get_terminal is get-or-create and would\nspawn a terminal for an unknown name, breaking GET /api/terminals for\nevery client. A stored terminal colour now carries that fingerprint and\nis dropped as soon as it stops matching, so a recycled name starts clear.\n\nAn entry with no fingerprint cannot be told apart from the stale entry\nthis exists to remove, so the upgrade clears terminal tab colours once.\nFile tabs are keyed by path and are untouched.\n\nCI gains pytest, the server-extension presence check and an endpoint\nauthentication gate. Makefile updated to the canonical 1.37.","tree":{"sha":"c37baae804b741f8ce2d637020ab2d1a7872a9c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stellarshenson/jupyterlab_colourful_tab_extension/git/trees/c37baae804b741f8ce2d637020ab2d1a7872a9c0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stellarshenson/jupyterlab_colourful_tab_extension/git/commits/1f2fb244dad55f343cad9490ed05341d95b82529","verification":{"payload":null,"