ubscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stellarshenson/jupyterlab_colourful_tab_extension/commits/098756d24fc2bc4f7d0639deda7834acf2dfc5a0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-17T12:38:17Z","email":"konrad.jelen@gmail.com","name":"stellarshenson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-17T12:38:17Z","email":"konrad.jelen@gmail.com","name":"stellarshenson"},"message":"feat: divider contrast setting + exclude active tab from divider (DEF-7)\n\n- dividerContrast setting (low 3:1 / medium 4:1 / high 6:1, default\n  medium - the previous fixed behaviour): CONTRAST_TARGETS maps the\n  magnitude to the target ratio, asDividerContrast guards raw settings\n  values by deriving membership from the map\n- the divider no longer recolours a seam touching the selected tab:\n  :not(.lm-mod-current) on both neighbours - the active tab is already\n  distinguished by its own -active shade, so the grey belongs only\n  between two inactive same-coloured tabs (DEF-7); greys are computed\n  against the inactive shade only, since the active shade can no longer\n  touch a divider\n- dividerGrey target parameter is now required - the magnitude-to-ratio\n  mapping lives in one place, a default would be a driftable copy\n- adversarially reviewed (architect + bug-hunter, two rounds): the\n  anti-drift net now pins CONTRAST_TARGETS values, the schema\n  description ratios, strict all-colour monotonicity and both clamp\n  directions; a guard test keeps the :not on every divider rule\n- DEF-7 registered in docs/defects.md with live pixel verification","tree":{"sha":"1e2cb5fdafba4cdc6e2da7531341849c4dd0a9cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stellarshenson/jupyterlab_colourful_tab_extension/git/trees/1e2cb5fdafba4cdc6e2da7531341849c4dd0a9cb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stellarshenson/jupyterlab_co