tml_url":"https://github.com/Luciano0322/signal-kernel/commit/adc91795f62072fb3375379b802650537d10c962","sha":"adc91795f62072fb3375379b802650537d10c962","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Luciano0322/signal-kernel/commits/adc91795f62072fb3375379b802650537d10c962"}],"sha":"fbe5816c6edc28b54cdb66270115b92da766a672","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Luciano0322/signal-kernel/commits/fbe5816c6edc28b54cdb66270115b92da766a672"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/62631200?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Luciano0322/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Luciano0322/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Luciano0322/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Luciano0322/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Luciano0322","id":62631200,"login":"Luciano0322","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyNjMxMjAw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Luciano0322/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Luciano0322/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Luciano0322/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Luciano0322/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Luciano0322/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Luciano0322","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Luciano0322/signal-kernel/commits/adc91795f62072fb3375379b802650537d10c962/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T09:03:10Z","email":"62631200+Luciano0322@users.noreply.github.com","name":"LucianoLee"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T09:03:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Merge pull request #20 from Luciano0322/pkg_async\n\n## Summary\n\nExtend `createStreamResource` with framework-neutral lifecycle controls for long-lived push-based streams such as SSE, WebSocket, Observable, and event subscriptions.\n\nThis keeps the existing stream primitive while expanding it beyond finite AsyncIterable and LLM-style producers.\n## Adapter Ownership\n\nReact and Vue adapters continue exposing the original stream metadata without implicitly owning resource disposal.\n\nComponent unmount or Vue scope disposal does not automatically dispose a potentially shared graph resource. Applications may connect `meta.dispose()` to framework lifecycle when ownership is explicit.\n\n## Integration Proof\n\n- Move the Nuxt job monitor kernel-owned SSE subscription lifecycle into `createStreamResource`.\n- Keep EventSource construction inside the transport layer.\n- Verify listener cleanup, stale callback rejection, reconnect behavior, and snapshot restore.\n- Update the Hono job runtime to use `dispose()` when its runtime owner is destroyed.\n\n## Compatibility\n\nExisting finite and LLM-style stream producers remain compatible and do not need to use the new lifecycle APIs.\n\nCustom tests or wrappers that manually construct `StreamContext` or `StreamAsyncMeta` objects must add the newly required members.\n\n## Release\n\n- `@signal-kernel/async-runtime`: minor\n- `@signal-kernel/react`: patch\n- `@signal-kernel/vue`: patch\n- Updated examples: patch","tree":{"sha":"0952a91351a26f206a4d79f73f557aa527e7ae64","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Luciano0322/signal-kernel/git/trees/0952a91351a26f206a4d79f73f557aa527e7ae64"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Luciano0322/signal-kernel/git/commits/adc91795f62072fb3375379b802650537d10c962","verification":{"payload":"tree 0952a91351a26f206a4d79f73f557aa527e7ae64\nparent e0acd9015c14018cc949daf0e672aaed37aa4288\nparent a13ad9584b232db0d21345e0cb0341f431e1b649\nauthor LucianoLee <62631200+Luciano0322@users.noreply.github.com> 1786957390 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786957390 +0800\n\nMerge pull request #20 from Luciano0322/pkg_async\n\n## Summary\n\nExtend `createStreamResource` with framework-neutral lifecycle controls for long-lived push-based streams such as SSE, WebSocket, Observable, and event subscriptions.\n\nThis keeps the existing stream primitive while expanding it beyond finite AsyncIterable and LLM-style producers.\n## Adapter Ownership\n\nReact and Vue adapters continue exposing the original stream metadata without implicitly owning resource disposal.\n\nComponent unmount or Vue scope disposal does not automatically dispose a potentially shared graph resource. Applications may connect `meta.dispose()` to framework lifecycle when ownership is explicit.\n\n## Integration Proof\n\n- Move the Nuxt job monitor kernel-owned SSE subscription lifecycle into `createStreamResource`.\n- Keep EventSource construction inside the transport layer.\n- Verify listener cleanup, stale callback rejection, reconnect behavior, and snapshot restore.\n- Update the Hono job runtime to use `dispose()` when its runtime owner is destroyed.\n\n## Compatibility\n\nExisting finite and LLM-style stream producers remain compatible and do not need to use the new lifecycle APIs.\n\nCustom tests or wrappers that manually construct `StreamContext` or `StreamAsyncMeta` objects must add the newly required members.\n\n## Release\n\n- `@signal-kernel/async-runtime`: minor\n- `@signal-kernel/react`: patch\n- `@signal-kernel/vue`: patch\n- Updated examples: patch","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqgs5OCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsSQQABZX1V7pX98ZK2gq5uI0eVkg\nEEG+cvKin4edH3nX4qgrtoVSPq57UHfGc/A4ilI6NhltsXzCxabCvCWcgMknGnu+\nXVJD2RsH6leB9G2ETVoEQsg1C3PN2iCYUrLe17gKgU9f6BT6UguKjQwT+xY0BZgR\n65L5R4vcM9OpdUeyHXM9BoQkZFYK2V885GXFSpqZNaGdKw+on78StGbS1qBYLk4U\nw2BjKbBSIaO0gXZIuje1cJ0/Y7iGP30gdUDxjw4c3DxWjfyacZSZDXN0XrUq8yfd\nvAcIlO+QRktO6ROsp/HqpQeOZnl7Z+9gWVY32wsQEZ51FoCE69i5+7wRSNrZ6QT7\nEl3i4d776Gb+2LHYFeJvFMryYaBo/IwN7KfNsEykNePQkwNFS20WIYuwHwjTGl0y\nkLi1UlrVYPNF2H4GKLwQxQQZZKhL56i4ojfdDhiun97DVnnmeoJ+0jzNbm3Nlto2\nz+gGQBHsbw2vMjGOwAIg44D1Ku/kGzNJovEvZwiWxSdRGQMUI/vKH6r1J72gl24