s_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rollipop-dev/rollipop/commit/a4b4a32f2fddd179bff209d2e85034130d8c3141","node_id":"C_kwDOQijf2doAKGE0YjRhMzJmMmZkZGQxNzliZmYyMDlkMmU4NTAzNDEzMGQ4YzMxNDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rollipop-dev/rollipop/commit/babf84596ccaf43194d6389a10c16621a97bd66a","sha":"babf84596ccaf43194d6389a10c16621a97bd66a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rollipop-dev/rollipop/commits/babf84596ccaf43194d6389a10c16621a97bd66a"}],"sha":"a4b4a32f2fddd179bff209d2e85034130d8c3141","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rollipop-dev/rollipop/commits/a4b4a32f2fddd179bff209d2e85034130d8c3141"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29110?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/dependabot","id":49699333,"login":"dependabot[bot]","node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk2OTkzMzM=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rollipop-dev/rollipop/commits/babf84596ccaf43194d6389a10c16621a97bd66a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T09:30:01Z","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"dependabot[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T09:30:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(deps): bump hono from 4.13.1 to 4.13.9 (#192)\n\nBumps [hono](https://github.com/honojs/hono) from 4.13.1 to 4.13.9.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/honojs/hono/releases\">hono''s\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v4.13.9</h2>\n<h2>What''s Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>fix(jsx): replace Suspense and ErrorBoundary content across newlines\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5380\">honojs/hono#5380</a></li>\n<li>fix(accepts): match media types and language tags case-insensitively\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5376\">honojs/hono#5376</a></li>\n<li>fix(linear-router): don''t match an empty path segment as a param in\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5373\">honojs/hono#5373</a></li>\n<li>fix(pretty-json): don''t break responses with unparseable JSON bodies\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5377\">honojs/hono#5377</a></li>\n<li>fix(jwt): throw JwtTokenInvalid when the signature is not valid\nbase64url in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5379\">honojs/hono#5379</a></li>\n<li>fix(aws-lambda): treat binary +xml archive media types as binary in\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5424\">honojs/hono#5424</a></li>\n<li>fix(aws-lambda): preserve empty query parameters in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5292\">honojs/hono#5292</a></li>\n<li>fix(lambda-edge): sync content type detection with aws-lambda in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5426\">honojs/hono#5426</a></li>\n<li>fix(lambda-edge): fail with a descriptive error on a malformed event\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5358\">honojs/hono#5358</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/honojs/hono/compare/v4.13.8...v4.13.9\">https://github.com/honojs/hono/compare/v4.13.8...v4.13.9</a></p>\n<h2>v4.13.8</h2>\n<h2>What''s Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>docs: fix typos in code comments and link third-party middleware\nsection in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5343\">honojs/hono#5343</a></li>\n<li>perf(jsx/dom): reduce lookup work for large keyed updates in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5340\">honojs/hono#5340</a></li>\n<li>fix(aws-lambda): respect backpressure when streaming the response\nbody in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5351\">honojs/hono#5351</a></li>\n<li>fix(accepts, language): skip accept entries with quality 0 when\nmatching in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5311\">honojs/hono#5311</a></li>\n<li>fix(accept): treat the q parameter name as case-insensitive in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5349\">honojs/hono#5349</a></li>\n<li>fix(accept): clamp a negative q to 0, not 1 in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5357\">honojs/hono#5357</a></li>\n<li>fix(request): keep the request media type when reusing a cached body\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5366\">honojs/hono#5366</a></li>\n<li>docs(combine): fix except() JSDoc param and add missing <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/returns\"><code>@​returns</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5346\">honojs/hono#5346</a></li>\n<li>perf(jsx/dom): optimize matching-head child lookup during\nreconciliation in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5329\">honojs/hono#5329</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/honojs/hono/compare/v4.13.7...v4.13.8\">https://github.com/honojs/hono/compare/v4.13.7...v4.13.8</a></p>\n<h2>v4.13.7</h2>\n<h2>Security fixes</h2>\n<p>This release includes a fix for the following security issue:</p>\n<h3><code>hono/jsx</code> renders plain strings unescaped in boundary\ncomponents, leading to XSS</h3>\n<p>Affects: <code>Suspense</code>, <code>ErrorBoundary</code>, and\n<code>Context.Provider</code> in <code>hono/jsx</code>, and\n<code>renderToString()</code> / <code>renderToReadableStream()</code> in\n<code>hono/jsx/dom/server</code>. Fixes missing HTML escaping for a\nplain string placed directly as a child or <code>fallback</code> of\nthese components, or as the root value of the server rendering\nfunctions, so untrusted strings could be emitted as markup.\nGHSA-hxh3-vqpv-xpqv</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Users who render untrusted strings inside <code>Suspense</code>,\n<code>ErrorBoundary</code>, or <code>Context.Provider</code>, or pass\nthem directly to <code>hono/jsx/dom/server</code>, are strongly\nencouraged to upgrade to this version.</p>\n<h2>v4.13.6</h2>\n<h2>What''s Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>fix(client): keep a param value of &quot;index&quot; in $url() and\n$path() in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5297\">honojs/hono#5297</a></li>\n<li>fix(client): normalize root WebSocket URLs in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5291\">honojs/hono#5291</a></li>\n<li>fix(types): allow symbol keys in Context<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\nget and set fallbacks in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5300\">honojs/hono#5300</a></li>\n<li>chore: bump <code>editorconfig-checker</code> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5336\">honojs/hono#5336</a></li>\n<li>refactor(on-handler): use forEach for consistent handler iteration\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5326\">honojs/hono#5326</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/honojs/hono/compare/v4.13.5...v4.13.6\">https://github.com/honojs/hono/compare/v4.13.5...v4.13.6</a></p>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/honojs/hono/commit/7c3b0df96dbf3e767968ff5afe4c0d999257b8ee\"><code>7c3b0df</code></a>\n4.13.9</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/honojs/hono/commit/6cadf7537385c6e3df9cbd6d05c9b84c82ae0361\"><code>6cadf75</code></a>\nfix(lambda-edge): fail with a descriptive error on a malformed event (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/honojs/hono/issues/5358\">#5358</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/honojs/hono/commit/de310ac063febf3e7b73f6206142d0e88800661f\"><code>de310ac</code></a>\nfix(lambda-edge): sync content type detection with aws-lambda (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/honojs/hono/issues/5426\">#5426</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/honojs/hono/commit/28e8572cd265b4da1160ce6cd51919bb70516e2c\"><code>28e8572</code></a>\nfix(aws-lambda): preserve empty query parameters (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/honojs/hono/issues/5292\">#5292</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/honojs/hono/commit/0d86899d28e146da0c8760201b2d08ddae732eaa\"><code>0d86899</code></a>\nfix(aws-lambda): treat binary +xml archive media types as binary (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/honojs/hono/issues/5424\">#5424</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/honojs/hono/commit/52febbcc30bc509d5e4987577e63906fe08fc471\"><code>52febbc</code></a>\nfix(jwt): throw JwtTokenInvalid when the signature is not valid\nbase64url (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/honojs/hono/issues/5\">#5</a>...</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/honojs/hono/commit/f950277cd3d9264622785e82785f21c648da699a\"><code>f950277</code></a>\nfix(pretty-json): don''t break responses with unparseable JSON bodies (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/honojs/hono/issues/5377\">#5377</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/honojs/hono/commit/00ee875728e2369b98a9ab7dda0690b77afedcff\"><code>00ee875</code></a>\nfix(linear-router): don''t match an empty path segment as a param (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/honojs/hono/issues/5373\">#5373</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/honojs/hono/commit/f5a53463ad2ff791fc02418b645750ce75a260ad\"><code>f5a5346</code></a>\nfix(accepts): match media types and language tags case-insensitively (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/honojs/hono/issues/5376\">#5376</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/honojs/hono/commit/cb5bea3614e6591e8ab933ef9a38ce7addf1d09a\"><code>cb5bea3</code></a>\nfix(jsx): replace Suspense and ErrorBoundary content across newlines (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/honojs/hono/issues/5380\">#5380</a>)</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/honojs/hono/compare/v4.13.1...v4.13.9\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"06922126fd22ef71537d8861ef3ff2b760c465c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rollipop-dev/rollipop/git/trees/06922126fd22ef71537d8861ef3ff2b760c465c4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rollipop-dev/rollipop/git/commits/babf84596ccaf43194d6389a10c16621a97bd66a","verification":{"payload":"tree 06922126fd22ef71537d8861ef3ff2b760c465c4\nparent 23dd787f747d6de6309e49f41d11f5db4a1314a9\nauthor dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1790847001 +0900\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790847001 +0900\n\nchore(deps): bump hono from 4.13.1 to 4.13.9 (#192)\n\nBumps [hono](https://github.com/honojs/hono) from 4.13.1 to 4.13.9.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/honojs/hono/releases\">hono''s\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v4.13.9</h2>\n<h2>What''s Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>fix(jsx): replace Suspense and ErrorBoundary content across newlines\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5380\">honojs/hono#5380</a></li>\n<li>fix(accepts): match media types and language tags case-insensitively\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5376\">honojs/hono#5376</a></li>\n<li>fix(linear-router): don''t match an empty path segment as a param in\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5373\">honojs/hono#5373</a></li>\n<li>fix(pretty-json): don''t break responses with unparseable JSON bodies\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5377\">honojs/hono#5377</a></li>\n<li>fix(jwt): throw JwtTokenInvalid when the signature is not valid\nbase64url in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5379\">honojs/hono#5379</a></li>\n<li>fix(aws-lambda): treat binary +xml archive media types as binary in\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5424\">honojs/hono#5424</a></li>\n<li>fix(aws-lambda): preserve empty query parameters in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5292\">honojs/hono#5292</a></li>\n<li>fix(lambda-edge): sync content type detection with aws-lambda in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5426\">honojs/hono#5426</a></li>\n<li>fix(lambda-edge): fail with a descriptive error on a malformed event\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5358\">honojs/hono#5358</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/honojs/hono/compare/v4.13.8...v4.13.9\">https://github.com/honojs/hono/compare/v4.13.8...v4.13.9</a></p>\n<h2>v4.13.8</h2>\n<h2>What''s Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>docs: fix typos in code comments and link third-party middleware\nsection in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5343\">honojs/hono#5343</a></li>\n<li>perf(jsx/dom): reduce lookup work for large keyed updates in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5340\">honojs/hono#5340</a></li>\n<li>fix(aws-lambda): respect backpressure when streaming the response\nbody in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5351\">honojs/hono#5351</a></li>\n<li>fix(accepts, language): skip accept entries with quality 0 when\nmatching in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5311\">honojs/hono#5311</a></li>\n<li>fix(accept): treat the q parameter name as case-insensitive in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5349\">honojs/hono#5349</a></li>\n<li>fix(accept): clamp a negative q to 0, not 1 in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5357\">honojs/hono#5357</a></li>\n<li>fix(request): keep the request media type when reusing a cached body\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5366\">honojs/hono#5366</a></li>\n<li>docs(combine): fix except() JSDoc param and add missing <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/returns\"><code>@​returns</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5346\">honojs/hono#5346</a></li>\n<li>perf(jsx/dom): optimize matching-head child lookup during\nreconciliation in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5329\">honojs/hono#5329</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/honojs/hono/compare/v4.13.7...v4.13.8\">https://github.com/honojs/hono/compare/v4.13.7...v4.13.8</a></p>\n<h2>v4.13.7</h2>\n<h2>Security fixes</h2>\n<p>This release includes a fix for the following security issue:</p>\n<h3><code>hono/jsx</code> renders plain strings unescaped in boundary\ncomponents, leading to XSS</h3>\n<p>Affects: <code>Suspense</code>, <code>ErrorBoundary</code>, and\n<code>Context.Provider</code> in <code>hono/jsx</code>, and\n<code>renderToString()</code> / <code>renderToReadableStream()</code> in\n<code>hono/jsx/dom/server</code>. Fixes missing HTML escaping for a\nplain string placed directly as a child or <code>fallback</code> of\nthese components, or as the root value of the server rendering\nfunctions, so untrusted strings could be emitted as markup.\nGHSA-hxh3-vqpv-xpqv</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Users who render untrusted strings inside <code>Suspense</code>,\n<code>ErrorBoundary</code>, or <code>Context.Provider</code>, or pass\nthem directly to <code>hono/jsx/dom/server</code>, are strongly\nencouraged to upgrade to this version.</p>\n<h2>v4.13.6</h2>\n<h2>What''s Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>fix(client): keep a param value of &quot;index&quot; in $url() and\n$path() in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5297\">honojs/hono#5297</a></li>\n<li>fix(client): normalize root WebSocket URLs in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5291\">honojs/hono#5291</a></li>\n<li>fix(types): allow symbol keys in Context<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\nget and set fallbacks in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5300\">honojs/hono#5300</a></li>\n<li>chore: bump <code>editorconfig-checker</code> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5336\">honojs/hono#5336</a></li>\n<li>refactor(on-handler): use forEach for consistent handler iteration\nin <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5326\">honojs/hono#5326</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/honojs/hono/compare/v4.13.5...v4.13.6\">https://github.com/honojs/hono/compare/v4.13.5...v4.13.6</a></p>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (tr