.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dependabot%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rollipop-dev/rollipop/commits/86e8c8ddb188538e81c27d5f72ddeecf6cd8369c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T02:40:34Z","email":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"dependabot[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T02:40:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(deps): bump undici from 7.29.0 to 7.29.1 (#188)\n\nBumps [undici](https://github.com/nodejs/undici) from 7.29.0 to 7.29.1.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/releases\">undici''s\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v7.29.1</h2>\n<h2>⚠️ Security fixes</h2>\n<h3>High severity</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/security/advisories/GHSA-w293-vg96-wgc3\">GHSA-w293-vg96-wgc3</a>:\n<code>BalancedPool</code> could drop function-valued connection options\nwhile cloning its configuration, including custom TLS certificate\nvalidation callbacks. Undici now preserves <code>connect</code> and\nlegacy <code>tls</code> options when creating upstreams. Fixed by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/f690157d728508652fef14673630c71515123e96\">f690157d</a>.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/security/advisories/GHSA-rfgv-xxqx-mfg5\">GHSA-rfgv-xxqx-mfg5</a>:\na WebSocket server could select a subprotocol when none was requested,\ncausing an uncaught <code>TypeError</code> that could terminate the\nprocess. Undici now rejects the handshake with protocol error 1002.\nFixed by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/6615e0175e9b635bcd2e3e87a47daa82f6f5b728\">6615e017</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Medium severity</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/security/advisories/GHSA-3wwx-pv8p-q78v\">GHSA-3wwx-pv8p-q78v</a>:\na malformed permessage-deflate payload exceeding the configured\ndecompression limit could emit an unhandled zlib error and terminate the\nprocess. Undici now destroys the inflater after reaching the limit.\nFixed by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/63cf698b611fecc6ee0a17b185b930051e4b982f\">63cf698b</a>.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/security/advisories/GHSA-rx4f-c7p8-82vq\">GHSA-rx4f-c7p8-82vq</a>:\nan unclean <code>WebSocketStream</code> close could create an unobserved\nrejected promise when its writable stream was locked, potentially\nterminating the process. Undici now propagates the failure through the\nretained writable stream controller. Fixed by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/1858656ebb1e919311c1f31613dfd581b7214349\">1858656e</a>.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/security/advisories/GHSA-2jfj-6hjv-fm6j\">GHSA-2jfj-6hjv-fm6j</a>:\nshared caches could store and replay responses containing\n<code>Set-Cookie</code>, disclosing one user''s cookies to another\ncaller. Undici now excludes these responses from shared caches,\nincluding existing entries and revalidation paths. Fixed by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/b6c5a00252c37da9dd2db9bead053bb843e1f988\">b6c5a002</a>.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/security/advisories/GHSA-3xpg-4rpp-hhhm\">GHSA-3xpg-4rpp-hhhm</a>:\nthe decompression interceptor did not bound decoded output, allowing\ncompressed responses to consume excessive memory. Undici now limits\nevery decompression stage to 64 MiB by default and supports a\nconfigurable <code>maxSize</code>. Fixed by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/2c7d7e1227043c644c4c32cfd1e276f4fd4fcb11\">2c7d7e12</a>.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/security/advisories/GHSA-pmjh-fq2x-6v4x\">GHSA-pmjh-fq2x-6v4x</a>:\na terminal retry failure after response headers were exposed could\norphan the original response body, causing consumers to hang\nindefinitely. Undici now propagates the terminal error to the exposed\nbody. Fixed by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/3c6726599cea8646384dde846c97d630da472a74\">3c672659</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Low severity</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/security/advisories/GHSA-8436-99hf-9mmv\">GHSA-8436-99hf-9mmv</a>:\ncache interceptors could store and replay responses to unsafe HTTP\nmethods such as <code>POST</code> or <code>DELETE</code>. Undici now\nrestricts cache reads and writes to safe methods while preserving\ninvalidation by successful unsafe requests. Fixed by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/b61d9432bac7caac51273ad209862e4c0bf935ae\">b61d9432</a>.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/security/advisories/GHSA-2gqq-gqf2-x968\">GHSA-2gqq-gqf2-x968</a>:\nthe dump interceptor could treat an oversized chunked response as\nsuccessfully truncated when no <code>Content-Length</code> was present.\nUndici now enforces <code>maxSize</code> against received bytes and\naborts oversized responses. Fixed by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/21693f406f0142f3504192e9f9b022dcf84782ae\">21693f40</a>.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/security/advisories/GHSA-r53p-7pc4-xj5r\">GHSA-r53p-7pc4-xj5r</a>:\nthe retry interceptor could concatenate a resumed response with\ninconsistent framing into downstream output, enabling response splitting\nor corruption. Undici now validates <code>Content-Range</code> against\nthe original response framing before resuming. Fixed by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/cd8af90b38ae33c2838d54a2d629774122effe95\">cd8af90b</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>What''s Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>[v7.x] drop: remove Node.js 26 from shared-builtin CI build by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/mcollina\"><code>@​mcollina</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/nodejs/undici/pull/5592\">nodejs/undici#5592</a></li>\n<li>fix(h2): honour headersTimeout by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/mcollina\"><code>@​mcollina</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/nodejs/undici/pull/5604\">nodejs/undici#5604</a></li>\n<li>fix(h2): keep the connection ref''d while requests are outstanding by\n<a href=\"https://github.com/mcollina\"><code>@​mcollina</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/nodejs/undici/pull/5605\">nodejs/undici#5605</a></li>\n<li>ci: increase Windows workflow timeout on v7.x by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/mcollina\"><code>@​mcollina</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/nodejs/undici/pull/5621\">nodejs/undici#5621</a></li>\n<li>fix(h2): retire the request that completed, not the head of the\nqueue by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/mcollina\"><code>@​mcollina</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/nodejs/undici/pull/5618\">nodejs/undici#5618</a></li>\n<li>fix(h2): settle a request whose stream is cancelled by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/mcollina\"><code>@​mcollina</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/nodejs/undici/pull/5607\">nodejs/undici#5607</a></li>\n<li>perf: reduce EventSourceStream parser allocations (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/nodejs/undici/issues/5032\">#5032</a>)\nby <a href=\"https://github.com/mcollina\"><code>@​mcollina</code></a> in\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/nodejs/undici/pull/5646\">nodejs/undici#5646</a></li>\n<li>fix(h2): handle GOAWAY for CONNECT streams by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/mcollina\"><code>@​mcollina</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/nodejs/undici/pull/5640\">nodejs/undici#5640</a></li>\n<li>[v7.x] perf(h1): drop idle-socket timer floor with a ref''d\nsetImmediate (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/nodejs/undici/issues/5707\">#5707</a>)\nby <a href=\"https://github.com/mcollina\"><code>@​mcollina</code></a> in\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/nodejs/undici/pull/5769\">nodejs/undici#5769</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/compare/v7.29.0...v7.29.1\">https://github.com/nodejs/undici/compare/v7.29.0...v7.29.1</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/d39a83e7b0d631590c3b85b5cc0dbeab66c3a1d8\"><code>d39a83e</code></a>\nBumped v7.29.1 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/nodejs/undici/issues/5772\">#5772</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/0d88464876d02bdb9cf27015d9d66500a8aaa782\"><code>0d88464</code></a>\nfix(test): remove unused EventEmitter import</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/f57411b894d45b89964252971497507500c32bc1\"><code>f57411b</code></a>\nperf(h1): drop idle-socket timer floor with a ref''d setImmediate (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/nodejs/undici/issues/5707\">#5707</a>)\n(<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/nodejs/undici/issues/5769\">#5769</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/3c6726599cea8646384dde846c97d630da472a74\"><code>3c67265</code></a>\nfix(retry): settle exposed body on terminal failure</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/cd8af90b38ae33c2838d54a2d629774122effe95\"><code>cd8af90</code></a>\nfix(retry): validate resumed response framing</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/6615e0175e9b635bcd2e3e87a47daa82f6f5b728\"><code>6615e01</code></a>\nfix(websocket): reject unrequested subprotocols</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/2c7d7e1227043c644c4c32cfd1e276f4fd4fcb11\"><code>2c7d7e1</code></a>\nfix(decompress): limit decompressed response size</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/b6c5a00252c37da9dd2db9bead053bb843e1f988\"><code>b6c5a00</code></a>\nfix(cache): do not cache Set-Cookie in shared caches</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/21693f406f0142f3504192e9f9b022dcf84782ae\"><code>21693f4</code></a>\nfix(interceptor/dump): abort oversized chunked responses</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/f690157d728508652fef14673630c71515123e96\"><code>f690157</code></a>\nfix: preserve BalancedPool connection options</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/compare/v7.29.0...v7.29.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=undici&package-manager=npm_and_yarn&previous-version=7.29.0&new-version=7.29.1)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don''t\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore this major version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this major version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this minor version` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this minor version (unless you reopen\nthe PR or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore this dependency` will close this PR and stop\nDependabot creating any more for this dependency (unless you reopen the\nPR or upgrade to it yourself)\nYou can disable automated security fix PRs for this repo from the\n[Security Alerts\npage](https://github.com/rollipop-dev/rollipop/network/alerts).\n\n</details>\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"91af25f670e3c6d4da91167f77ba2b17e8313238","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rollipop-dev/rollipop/git/trees/91af25f670e3c6d4da91167f77ba2b17e8313238"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rollipop-dev/rollipop/git/commits/86e8c8ddb188538e81c27d5f72ddeecf6cd8369c","verification":{"payload":"tree 91af25f670e3c6d4da91167f77ba2b17e8313238\nparent 5a97444876832f5a3c46e4a239cc34855224c16a\nauthor dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1790736034 +0900\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790736034 +0900\n\nchore(deps): bump undici from 7.29.0 to 7.29.1 (#188)\n\nBumps [undici](https://github.com/nodejs/undici) from 7.29.0 to 7.29.1.\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/releases\">undici''s\nreleases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v7.29.1</h2>\n<h2>⚠️ Security fixes</h2>\n<h3>High severity</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/security/advisories/GHSA-w293-vg96-wgc3\">GHSA-w293-vg96-wgc3</a>:\n<code>BalancedPool</code> could drop function-valued connection options\nwhile cloning its configuration, including custom TLS certificate\nvalidation callbacks. Undici now preserves <code>connect</code> and\nlegacy <code>tls</code> options when creating upstreams. Fixed by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/f690157d728508652fef14673630c71515123e96\">f690157d</a>.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/security/advisories/GHSA-rfgv-xxqx-mfg5\">GHSA-rfgv-xxqx-mfg5</a>:\na WebSocket server could select a subprotocol when none was requested,\ncausing an uncaught <code>TypeError</code> that could terminate the\nprocess. Undici now rejects the handshake with protocol error 1002.\nFixed by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/6615e0175e9b635bcd2e3e87a47daa82f6f5b728\">6615e017</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Medium severity</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/security/advisories/GHSA-3wwx-pv8p-q78v\">GHSA-3wwx-pv8p-q78v</a>:\na malformed permessage-deflate payload exceeding the configured\ndecompression limit could emit an unhandled zlib error and terminate the\nprocess. Undici now destroys the inflater after reaching the limit.\nFixed by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/63cf698b611fecc6ee0a17b185b930051e4b982f\">63cf698b</a>.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/security/advisories/GHSA-rx4f-c7p8-82vq\">GHSA-rx4f-c7p8-82vq</a>:\nan unclean <code>WebSocketStream</code> close could create an unobserved\nrejected promise when its writable stream was locked, potentially\nterminating the process. Undici now propagates the failure through the\nretained writable stream controller. Fixed by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/1858656ebb1e919311c1f31613dfd581b7214349\">1858656e</a>.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/security/advisories/GHSA-2jfj-6hjv-fm6j\">GHSA-2jfj-6hjv-fm6j</a>:\nshared caches could store and replay responses containing\n<code>Set-Cookie</code>, disclosing one user''s cookies to another\ncaller. Undici now excludes these responses from shared caches,\nincluding existing entries and revalidation paths. Fixed by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/b6c5a00252c37da9dd2db9bead053bb843e1f988\">b6c5a002</a>.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/security/advisories/GHSA-3xpg-4rpp-hhhm\">GHSA-3xpg-4rpp-hhhm</a>:\nthe decompression interceptor did not bound decoded output, allowing\ncompressed responses to consume excessive memory. Undici now limits\nevery decompression stage to 64 MiB by default and supports a\nconfigurable <code>maxSize</code>. Fixed by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/2c7d7e1227043c644c4c32cfd1e276f4fd4fcb11\">2c7d7e12</a>.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/security/advisories/GHSA-pmjh-fq2x-6v4x\">GHSA-pmjh-fq2x-6v4x</a>:\na terminal retry failure after response headers were exposed could\norphan the original response body, causing consumers to hang\nindefinitely. Undici now propagates the terminal error to the exposed\nbody. Fixed by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/3c6726599cea8646384dde846c97d630da472a74\">3c672659</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Low severity</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/security/advisories/GHSA-8436-99hf-9mmv\">GHSA-8436-99hf-9mmv</a>:\ncache interceptors could store and replay responses to unsafe HTTP\nmethods such as <code>POST</code> or <code>DELETE</code>. Undici now\nrestricts cache reads and writes to safe methods while preserving\ninvalidation by successful unsafe requests. Fixed by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/b61d9432bac7caac51273ad209862e4c0bf935ae\">b61d9432</a>.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/security/advisories/GHSA-2gqq-gqf2-x968\">GHSA-2gqq-gqf2-x968</a>:\nthe dump interceptor could treat an oversized chunked response as\nsuccessfully truncated when no <code>Content-Length</code> was present.\nUndici now enforces <code>maxSize</code> against received bytes and\naborts oversized responses. Fixed by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/21693f406f0142f3504192e9f9b022dcf84782ae\">21693f40</a>.</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/security/advisories/GHSA-r53p-7pc4-xj5r\">GHSA-r53p-7pc4-xj5r</a>:\nthe retry interceptor could concatenate a resumed response with\ninconsistent framing into downstream output, enabling response splitting\nor corruption. Undici now validates <code>Content-Range</code> against\nthe original response framing before resuming. Fixed by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/cd8af90b38ae33c2838d54a2d629774122effe95\">cd8af90b</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>What''s Changed</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>[v7.x] drop: remove Node.js 26 from shared-builtin CI build by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/mcollina\"><code>@​mcollina</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/nodejs/undici/pull/5592\">nodejs/undici#5592</a></li>\n<li>fix(h2): honour headersTimeout by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/mcollina\"><code>@​mcollina</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/nodejs/undici/pull/5604\">nodejs/undici#5604</a></li>\n<li>fix(h2): keep the connection ref''d while requests are outstanding by\n<a href=\"https://github.com/mcollina\"><code>@​mcollina</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/nodejs/undici/pull/5605\">nodejs/undici#5605</a></li>\n<li>ci: increase Windows workflow timeout on v7.x by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/mcollina\"><code>@​mcollina</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/nodejs/undici/pull/5621\">nodejs/undici#5621</a></li>\n<li>fix(h2): retire the request that completed, not the head of the\nqueue by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/mcollina\"><code>@​mcollina</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/nodejs/undici/pull/5618\">nodejs/undici#5618</a></li>\n<li>fix(h2): settle a request whose stream is cancelled by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/mcollina\"><code>@​mcollina</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/nodejs/undici/pull/5607\">nodejs/undici#5607</a></li>\n<li>perf: reduce EventSourceStream parser allocations (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/nodejs/undici/issues/5032\">#5032</a>)\nby <a href=\"https://github.com/mcollina\"><code>@​mcollina</code></a> in\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/nodejs/undici/pull/5646\">nodejs/undici#5646</a></li>\n<li>fix(h2): handle GOAWAY for CONNECT streams by <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/mcollina\"><code>@​mcollina</code></a> in <a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/nodejs/undici/pull/5640\">nodejs/undici#5640</a></li>\n<li>[v7.x] perf(h1): drop idle-socket timer floor with a ref''d\nsetImmediate (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/nodejs/undici/issues/5707\">#5707</a>)\nby <a href=\"https://github.com/mcollina\"><code>@​mcollina</code></a> in\n<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/nodejs/undici/pull/5769\">nodejs/undici#5769</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/compare/v7.29.0...v7.29.1\">https://github.com/nodejs/undici/compare/v7.29.0...v7.29.1</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/d39a83e7b0d631590c3b85b5cc0dbeab66c3a1d8\"><code>d39a83e</code></a>\nBumped v7.29.1 (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/nodejs/undici/issues/5772\">#5772</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/0d88464876d02bdb9cf27015d9d66500a8aaa782\"><code>0d88464</code></a>\nfix(test): remove unused EventEmitter import</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/f57411b894d45b89964252971497507500c32bc1\"><code>f57411b</code></a>\nperf(h1): drop idle-socket timer floor with a ref''d setImmediate (<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/nodejs/undici/issues/5707\">#5707</a>)\n(<a\nhref=\"https://redirect.github.com/nodejs/undici/issues/5769\">#5769</a>)</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/3c6726599cea8646384dde846c97d630da472a74\"><code>3c67265</code></a>\nfix(retry): settle exposed body on terminal failure</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/cd8af90b38ae33c2838d54a2d629774122effe95\"><code>cd8af90</code></a>\nfix(retry): validate resumed response framing</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/6615e0175e9b635bcd2e3e87a47daa82f6f5b728\"><code>6615e01</code></a>\nfix(websocket): reject unrequested subprotocols</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/2c7d7e1227043c644c4c32cfd1e276f4fd4fcb11\"><code>2c7d7e1</code></a>\nfix(decompress): limit decompressed response size</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/b6c5a00252c37da9dd2db9bead053bb843e1f988\"><code>b6c5a00</code></a>\nfix(cache): do not cache Set-Cookie in shared caches</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/21693f406f0142f3504192e9f9b022dcf84782ae\"><code>21693f4</code></a>\nfix(interceptor/dump): abort oversized chunked responses</li>\n<li><a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/f690157d728508652fef14673630c71515123e96\"><code>f690157</code></a>\nfix: preserve BalancedPool connection options</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a\nhref=\"https://github.com/nodejs/undici/compare/v7.29.0...v7.29.1\">compare\nview</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\n[![Dependabot compatibility\nscore](https://dependabot-badges.githubapp.com/badges/compatibility_score?dependency-name=undici&package-manager=npm_and_yarn&previous-version=7.29.0&new-version=7.29.1)](https://docs.github.com/en/github/managing-security-vulnerabilities/about-dependabot-security-updates#about-compatibility-scores)\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don''t\nalter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting\n`@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits\nthat have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all\nof the ignore conditions of the specified depe