:"https://api.github.com/repos/openmfp/create-micro-frontend/commits/fab03dac49fd13da9a01af734985e6a026b2098c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7794387?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gkrajniak","id":7794387,"login":"gkrajniak","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3OTQzODc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmfp/create-micro-frontend/commits/797c96cfd817164b718a611aa90588451709def9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T09:29:57Z","email":"gkrajniak@gmail.com","name":"Grzegorz Krajniak"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T09:29:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(deps): resolve all npm audit vulnerabilities (#23)\n\nClear all 7 reported advisories (1 critical, 4 high, 2 moderate) down to 0:\n- `npm audit fix` resolves the safely-fixable transitive advisories\n  (nanoid, postcss, rollup).\n- Bump vitest ^1.6.0 -> ^4.1.10 to drop the vulnerable esbuild/vite/\n  vite-node/vitest chain (the critical + remaining high/moderate).\n\nAll affected packages are dev-only (vitest test toolchain); the production\ndependency tree (`npm audit --omit=dev`) was already clean, so consumers of\nthe published CLI were never exposed.\n\nVerified: `npm audit` = 0, unit tests pass (12), tsc compiles. The vitest\nconfig uses only options still valid in v4.\n\nSigned-off-by: gkrajniak <gkrajniak@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"d18ea0d693a3a0b2032cd8097fd0c818e8a80d74","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmfp/create-micro-frontend/git/trees/d18ea0d693a3a0b2032cd8097fd0c818e8a80d74"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmfp/create-micro-frontend/git/commits/797c96cfd817164b718a611aa90588451709def9","verification":{"payload":"tree d18ea0d693a3a0b2032cd8097fd0c818e8a80d74\nparent f32098b9412f194a1195e4acb62e4ab60991e57b\nauthor Grzegorz Krajniak <gkrajniak@gmail.com> 1786958997 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786958997 +0200\n\nfix(deps): resolve all npm audit vulnerabilities (#23)\n\nClear all 7 reported advisories (1 critical, 4 high, 2 moderate) down to 0:\n- `npm audit fix` resolves the safely-fixable transitive advisories\n  (nanoid, postcss, rollup).\n- Bump vitest ^1.6.0 -> ^4.1.10 to drop the vulnerable esbuild/vite/\n  vite-node/vitest chain (the critical + remaining high/moderate).\n\nAll affected packages are dev-only (vitest test toolchain); the production\ndependency tree (`npm audit --omit=dev`) was already clean, so consumers of\nthe published CLI were never exposed.\n\nVerified: `npm audit` = 0, unit tests pass (12), tsc compiles. The vitest\nconfig uses only options still valid in v4.\n\nSigned-off-by: gkrajniak <gkrajniak@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqgtSVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOT8QAB8Q1msKisM3FxeX2prexZwM\npLkF/ZPmvsFWrcJvK5BYLSHjEnizTvZS4zz7MD/Ury1cIFSgyNiefuJX7DGEBPoD\nAT2+PmtiP1biYXrFOPkItDeIK8E9u6nPy8uuj7FjX/aTPBot7z2HNFxtA37MoB8G\noWaJBSINHfoJnmLGPGxyp345DCOreakeFvmd6IvSCF0cISobMc8U6PIoP5C1jKS+\n2mMLn1+3pwNYi4idbLPxNOdXhVtamZIuqdus9Qwx4ggFF8A7n2glC6Q+MV627WbP\nY7b7EaNmVZn0iBUDaWHHDOiI4reEiV+VysKImvaKLkUcHZzsok6g34I9XCh/LKx7\nISjyVB0646EBacL+OnXgoKyAD5gaiIcQHEaoa+I4T0auxwILe3R9mj37ioXvu2Zu\n+Xd7fdPG8uOPjKbNuI6BzpgndAUtT5E